+ * slot that the CPU fills with the resume value, so the GPU never parks on the
+ * shared event and resumes within a memory round trip. Parked on the event,
+ * the GPU also looked idle to the power manager during each expert call: with
+ * a 2.9 ms call the dense part of a layer took 1.45 ms instead of 0.50 (a
+ * side-queue keep-alive as in TP recovered only part of it and slowed short
+ * calls). FRONK_EVENT_RESUME=1 keeps the event wait. */
